# Our picture frontend cache: a request carries its whole conversation and every picture in it used to be decoded,
# fitted and hashed again on every turn. Measured on two Sparks, 1920x1080 PNGs, prompt hot, engine prefill taken
# out: 29.8 ms a picture -- 70 pictures 2.43 s of the first token before the engine saw the prompt. What reading a
# source cost is remembered, keyed by the source's bytes: a later turn hands back the row count and the key without
# reading it again. Host memory only; TENSORFOLD_GLM_PICTURE_CACHE=0 turns it off, ..._MB caps the source bytes.
# vision/glm.py is identical in the v0.6.0-5e01f1bb74d8 and v0.6.0-9f73cca659a1 images; verified against both.
# Apache-2.0.

